& [Host]
  + EVO-X2 is the exact remote Windows machine reached by the reviewed SSH alias; the alias alone does not prove host identity
& [CurrentBuild]
  + selected binaries are freshly rebuilt from the exact published checkout and content-addressed; an old target file is not accepted as provenance
& [CantorHost]
  + P0 means a versioned root capable of executing current governed Cantor contracts, not a resident daemon autonomous employee or production trust root
& [RunOurBuild]
  + P0 runs a current-build independent evidence contract; it does not yet compile the Cantor source tree or let Cantor change that tree
& [Isolation]
  + every transferred input and output lives under the new root and historical deployment roots remain byte-observed but unwritten
& [Determinism]
  + two fresh A8 processes produce the same canonical bytes; timing may differ and is not part of deterministic equality
& [Performance]
  + measured duration sizes exits and identities are local observations, not a model benchmark throughput guarantee or claim of faster inference
& [OptionalQuery]
  + a public query fixture runs only when all reads close inside the pilot; skipping is a valid truthful outcome
& [NoProvider]
  + the required A8 replay has zero model and network requests and does not depend on the existing llama.cpp listener
& [Preservation]
  + existing Needle2 attention SOP-agent llama.cpp model service and configuration identities must survive unchanged
& [Completion]
  + completion requires independent retrieved-evidence verification and idle closure, not merely a successful process exit
& [Frontier]
  + next compile a plan-only build contract; source mutation compilation commit publication self-update and persistent service operation require successor authority
